  "overview": "**Canvas Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#fcc6b1` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `HubSpot Serif` with `HubSpot Sans` body copy (112px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `#ffffff` -> `#f8f5ee` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Hubspot**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://canvas.hubspot.com/). Inventory: **91** colors, **24** typography steps, and **9** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 9 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f8f5ee` cards; separate sibling sections using `#f8f5ee` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#ffffff` -> `#f8f5ee`) and `1px solid #f8f5ee` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#fcc6b1` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#fcc6b1` with `#0b0b0c` text (13.0:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `HubSpot Serif` headings with `HubSpot Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f8f5ee` surface shifts and `#f8f5ee` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
